# Static files first.
/robots.txt     /robots.txt     200
/sitemap.xml    /sitemap.xml    200

# Deliberately NO per-route rules here.
#
# Prerendering writes one flat file per route (`directory.html`, `terms.html`, ...)
# and Cloudflare Pages already serves those for the extension-less URL
# (`/directory` -> `directory.html`). Adding a `200` rewrite for the same path does
# not help: Cloudflare normalises the rewritten `.html` target back to the
# extension-less form, which matches the rule again. The result is an infinite
# 308 loop where `/directory` redirects to `/directory`. `npm run build` now fails
# if a rule for a prerendered route reappears in this file.
#
# Anything not matching a prerendered route or a real asset falls through to
# 404.html with a real 404 status, rather than the old behaviour where every junk
# URL returned 200 with the homepage (a 'soft 404' that pollutes search results).

# /donate was a thin duplicate of /give with no inbound links. A 301 consolidates the
# two so search engines index one page instead of two competing ones.
/donate          /give           301
